# Checkout and diff attributes for inputs whose bytes are audited.
# Git text conversion can rewrite LF as CRLF on Windows and change a source digest,
# a Cargo checksum, a license bundle or an archive member. Keep the rules below exact;
# TestPinnedRustSourcesDisableGitTextConversion and TestReleaseLicenseOutputsUseLFCheckout
# assert them through `git check-attr`.

# Pinned Rust source identity. The staticlib source digest hashes Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock,
# an optional build.rs, .cargo/** and src/**/*.rs, so all of them keep their committed
# bytes. The build.rs rule covers the optional digest input even while the crate has no
# such file.
internal/media/ugoira/rust/Cargo.toml -text
internal/media/ugoira/rust/Cargo.lock -text
internal/media/ugoira/rust/build.rs -text
internal/media/ugoira/rust/.cargo/** -text
internal/media/ugoira/rust/src/**/*.rs -text

# Cargo vendor closure and the pinned local quantette source. Every file is fixed by its
# own .cargo-checksum.json; a CRLF checkout would make `cargo --locked --offline` reject
# an otherwise untouched dependency tree.
internal/media/ugoira/rust/vendor/** -text
third_party/rust/quantette-0.6.0/** -text

# cmd.exe cannot reliably parse an LF script, and the release tests disable autocrlf to
# preserve other audited inputs, so force CRLF only for this public installer.
scripts/install.cmd text eol=crlf

# Release license inputs are compared byte-for-byte by the archive and licensebundle
# gates. Fix LF so a Windows checkout cannot split cross-platform archive evidence or
# report an unmodified license bundle as stale.
LICENSE text eol=lf
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md text eol=lf
third_party/licenses/** text eol=lf

# Upstream conflict-marker false positives. These README headings use seven equals signs,
# which Git mistakes for an unresolved merge conflict; only the threshold is raised and
# the file bytes stay untouched.
internal/media/ugoira/rust/vendor/autocfg/README.md conflict-marker-size=32
internal/media/ugoira/rust/vendor/ref-cast/README.md conflict-marker-size=32

# Upstream whitespace overrides. These `cargo vendor --locked --offline` copies are pinned
# by their own .cargo-checksum.json and already carry whitespace warnings; rewriting a byte
# would make Cargo reject the vendor tree. Each rule names the exact file that triggers the
# check, so the rest of the repository keeps the default whitespace gate. Do not collapse
# this list into directory globs: that would silently exempt files that do not currently
# trigger a warning.
